{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":70965005,"ns":0,"title":"Appeal to the law","extract":"An appeal to the law (argumentum ad legem in Latin) is an informal fallacy in which someone tries to encourage or defend an action based on its legality, or condemn it as morally reprehensible, purely because it is illegal. This line of reasoning is faulty because although the law of the land is important, it does not necessarily match up with the morality or sensibility of an action.","description":"Type of logical fallacy","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}